{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound","id":1031018,"title":"[2E] Ochema and Bound","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-12T23:04:27-08:00","id":1031018,"title":"[2E] Ochema and Bound","content":"So how those 'mythical' beings should work in <b>Mage</b> 2E rules framework? I want my London game to return to plot with our Ochema of Abyss, I introduced before proper 2E and I'm just wondering how to bite this kind epic threats as rule systems.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: </b>In this topic, Ihammered some Numina for Supernal/Abyssal beings. Here are them:<br /> <br /> <b><i>Armor of Arcanum (Chosen Arcanum)</i></b><br /> <i>This being is protected by the power of Arcanum she is composed of. She is treated as having </i>Mage Armor Attainment <i>from chosen Arcanum, up to the level of her Arcana dots. Activating it for a scene is Reflexive Action. </i><i>In contrast to normal Mage Armor, being can benefit from multiple Mage Armor effect at once, if she have each </i>Armor of Arcanum<i> power for and she activated them first for the scene.</i><br /> <br /> <b><i>Body of God</i></b><br /> <i>This being is a \u2018shell\u2019 or physical manifestation of Supernal God. Those sub-souls are immune to simple destruction with only spells, as they need to return, again and again, to fulfill their once pointed purpose. Being cannot be killed with Aggravated damage \u2013 when she lose last point of Corpus, she reforms at nearest appropriate Supernal Verge after it\u2019s Rank in days, with Mana equal to her Rank. The only possible way to bypass this power is use of Bane for this being, as then death of it is permanent.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-11-2017, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T23:08:04-08:00","id":1031019,"title":"","content":"I think this is why Supernal Entity rules were added. Bound are &quot;just&quot; Rank 4-5 entities, and until Signs of Sorcery comes out with 2E rules for them, I would do the same thing for Ochema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T00:37:21-08:00","id":1031036,"title":"","content":"But Supernal Entities does 'puff' after limited time. And Bound or Ochema are not dispersing this easily from Fallen World. Maybe as Bound are hunting for Mana and Ochema are feed those by their creators ( are they? ) they do not have normal time limit of Supernal Beings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T01:17:53-08:00","id":1031037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1031036#post1031036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Supernal Entities does 'puff' after limited time. And Bound or Ochema are not dispersing this easily from Fallen World. Maybe as Bound are hunting for Mana and Ochema are feed those by their creators ( are they? ) they do not have normal time limit of Supernal Beings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal Verges allow Supernal beings to exist in a manifest state and reform within their bounds like ephemeral beings with appropriate Conditions. Exarchate Verges are notably the product of any Demesne made with a Prelacy 4 Seer's soul stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T01:44:55-08:00","id":1031046,"title":"","content":"Bound outside their Verge maintain their existence by Scouring the mana out of anything they come across. They target Mages specifically because there's usually a higher concentration of mana in their Patterns.<br /> <br /> For Ochema, what Satchel said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T11:18:59-08:00","id":1031258,"title":"","content":"Actually Bound hunt mana to stay awake, they slumber without it, but they are banned from the Supernal so they don't go puff or get eaten by the Abyss. When they get killed or run out of mana they just end up back in their Prison, making them one of the hardest things to permanently kill in the CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T11:31:15-08:00","id":1031267,"title":"","content":"It's likely the prison is a Verge though, there might be an actual rip to the Supernal at the center of it but that doesn't mean they can go through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T12:23:18-08:00","id":1031286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1031267#post1031267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's likely the prison is a Verge though, there might be an actual rip to the Supernal at the center of it but that doesn't mean they can go through it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ouch. Trapped for eternity, with only a little keyhole to see what is forever denied you.<br /> <br /> No wonder they are so foul tempered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T14:27:15-08:00","id":1031328,"title":"","content":"Ochema aren't Supernal entities, not in the traditional sense. While you can roughly model them the same way, they don't degrade outside of Verges. An Ochema is a purpose-built avatar of some transcendental being, like an Archmage or one of the Ascended; a thing they create that emanates of them and which they send into the world for a specific purpose. Their intended state of existence is in the Fallen World, not the Supernal Realms.<br /> <br /> If you want to use an ochema, build them as you would a Supernal entity but, instead of having their Mana tick away... Don't have that happen. And give them all the traits listed in the Seers of the Throne book.<br /> <br /> And above all else, for pity's sake, watch the fuck out if you pit one against anything less than a whole cabal of very high Gnosis Mages, because ochema by itself has a good shot of murdering everyone and everything around it. Even the weakest will see most spells bounce off of it like crumpled wads of tissue because their Withstand ratings are so ridiculously high.<br /> <br /> Don't fuck with a god, is what I am saying.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T14:40:31-08:00","id":1031334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1031328#post1031328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And above all else, for pity's sake, watch the fuck out if you pit one against anything less than a whole cabal of very high Gnosis Mages, because ochema by itself has a good shot of murdering everyone and everything around it. Even the weakest will see most spells bounce off of it like crumpled wads of tissue because their Withstand ratings are so ridiculously high.<br /> <br /> Don't fuck with a god, is what I am saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>My players cabal is 5-6 characters of Gnosis 6 and Master or Double Adept in Arcana. I think it's time to put them against Ochema. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( They also killed Royal Avatar ( Rank 5 ) of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895970-%E2%80%8B-2e-mystery-yellow-sign-hallows-network-corruption-and-abyssal-astral-realm\">Hastur</a> - bearly, but they did it. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T14:51:22-08:00","id":1031338,"title":"","content":"You might read Dave Brookshaw's actual plays to see how high rank things act. Ochema are not not just a monsters waiting in place for people to beat it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T15:01:12-08:00","id":1031341,"title":"","content":"Yeah, ochema are the extensions of the grandest minds in the cosmos. Unless they are presently out serving far from a major metropolitan area, an ochema is probably six or seven layers of conspiracy deep and bending every Seer pylon in the region to their will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T16:10:08-08:00","id":1031371,"title":"","content":"For Unbound I would use Dave's AP with the wyrm. It was pretty clearly limited to a specific area, but God help the Obrimos that tried to beat it...yeah, that worked out great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T22:02:25-08:00","id":1031449,"title":"","content":"Thing is not it's your typical Ochema - it's Ochema of Gate, Mistress of Abyss. Normal Ochema are Voices of Exarchs - and by this respected by any Seer. Ochema of Gate works for this Iron Seal you do not talk about - so I do not think, in the end, she will have as much 'social support' from Seers.<br /> <br /> As to mechanicly - I probably written her as Rank 5 Superal being, add Abyssal template and add Seers of Throne specific mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T03:27:19-08:00","id":1031518,"title":"","content":"The Ochemata of the Gate wouldn't need a Supernal Verge, just an Abyssal one. Good thing it's so easy to bring the Abyss into the world. Also Abyssal beings frequently don't seem to be stuck existing in a Verge, so an Ochemata of the gate doesn't really need a whole lot of social support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T07:19:41-08:00","id":1031571,"title":"","content":"Good point! Only it means that 'Biggest Abyssal Intruder we saw in our life!' Is raported across many Consilia in the world. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> 'She passed our lands - pray Oracles for who she goes after!'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-24-2017, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T09:27:28-08:00","id":1037253,"title":"","content":"Ochemata in <b>Seers of Throne</b> book has those special traits that I have problems with:<ul><li><i>Supernal Perfection</i>: They gain the rote quality (re-roll failed dice) - <b>Does this mean they get Rote Quality on Numina activation also?</b></li> <li><i>Magic</i>: Ochemata do not have Essence or Influences. Instead, they possess a Mana trait equivalent to Essence and have the same Arcana as Awakened mages (not just Influences that duplicate them). A lesser ochema is a Master in the Arcanum associated with its ruling Exarch. (For example, an ochema sent by the Eye has at least Space 5.) It usually possesses at least 5 other <br /> dots in additional Arcana. Greater ochema are even more powerful. <br /> Ochemata use Rank as their Gnosis. They know every rote related to their Exarch\u2019s primary Arcanum, but roll Power + Finesse + Arcanum for all spells, regardless of Arcanum. Ochemata can suffer Paradoxes and for this purpose are treated as if they had a Wisdom of 1.<br /> An ochema may possess a few Numina as well, but these are usually trivial compared to its magical abilities. - Here I have problem with Ochema of Gate - <b>Does it still should use Arcana? And I suppose that it's highest would be Influnace: Abyss simply, yes?</b></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T09:42:19-08:00","id":1037257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1037253#post1037253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ochemata in <b>Seers of Throne</b> book has those special traits that I have problems with:<ul><li><i>Supernal Perfection</i>: They gain the rote quality (re-roll failed dice) - <b>Does this mean they get Rote Quality on Numina activation also?</b></li> <li><i>Magic</i>: Ochemata do not have Essence or Influences. Instead, they possess a Mana trait equivalent to Essence and have the same Arcana as Awakened mages (not just Influences that duplicate them). A lesser ochema is a Master in the Arcanum associated with its ruling Exarch. (For example, an ochema sent by the Eye has at least Space 5.) It usually possesses at least 5 other<br /> dots in additional Arcana. Greater ochema are even more powerful.<br /> Ochemata use Rank as their Gnosis. They know every rote related to their Exarch\u2019s primary Arcanum, but roll Power + Finesse + Arcanum for all spells, regardless of Arcanum. Ochemata can suffer Paradoxes and for this purpose are treated as if they had a Wisdom of 1.<br /> An ochema may possess a few Numina as well, but these are usually trivial compared to its magical abilities. - Here I have problem with Ochema of Gate - <b>Does it still should use Arcana? And I suppose that it's highest would be Influnace: Abyss simply, yes?</b></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I would look at homebrew that treats the Abyss as an Arcana for an Ochemata of The Gate. Anything else is likely to be a disservice. Such as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/603390-homebrew-abyssal-arcanum\">this</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T10:12:28-08:00","id":1037271,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Ochemata should have Bans and Banes - they are manifestations of Exarch, they are bound by his wishes, don't they? On the other hand, they are simply summoned to the world with precise missions, not that they linger like normal ephemeral beings in Fallen World...<br /> <br /> If we <i>would</i> use Bans and Banes, what would be examples for those? Like for Ochema of Eye or ( if someone have idea ) mine Ochema of Gate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T10:35:48-08:00","id":1037285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1037271#post1037271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Ochemata should have Bans and Banes - they are manifestations of Exarch, they are bound by his wishes, don't they? On the other hand, they are simply summoned to the world with precise missions, not that they linger like normal ephemeral beings in Fallen World...<br /> <br /> If we <i>would</i> use Bans and Banes, what would be examples for those? Like for Ochema of Eye or ( if someone have idea ) mine Ochema of Gate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ban is easy enough - an inability to act against the will of the Exarch that created them (they are self-aware beings, so would have the capacity to do so, otherwise).<br /> Bane is harder...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T13:20:33-08:00","id":1037396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1037271#post1037271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Ochemata should have Bans and Banes - they are manifestations of Exarch, they are bound by his wishes, don't they? On the other hand, they are simply summoned to the world with precise missions, not that they linger like normal ephemeral beings in Fallen World...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like G-M Angels, and those have Bans and Banes.<br /> <br /> As for Banes, something from the legends about that Exarch? Or maybe an Artifact with greater than X dots? Especially for an Ochemata of the Abyss, I'd think concentrated Supernal Truth would be enough (so, Prime Artifact with &quot;enough&quot; dots?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:20:03-08:00","id":1037537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1037271#post1037271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Ochemata should have Bans and Banes - they are manifestations of Exarch, they are bound by his wishes, don't they? On the other hand, they are simply summoned to the world with precise missions, not that they linger like normal ephemeral beings in Fallen World...<br /> <br /> If we <i>would</i> use Bans and Banes, what would be examples for those? Like for Ochema of Eye or ( if someone have idea ) mine Ochema of Gate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bans would be submitting to the &quot;main body&quot;, like Inodiv said.<br /> <br /> My idea for banes would be something that symbolically defies straight the Exarch's symbolism. An Ochema of the Eye would be burned by something that symbolizes the value of freedom from surveillance, or something that proves that people can police themselves without outside intervention. Maybe the tears of a murderer who confessed his crimes when he could have gotten away perfectly from it? An Ochema of the Gate would be burned by something that reaffirms the truth, or proves that the world does not &quot;need&quot; the Abyss to be a better place. Something like the ashes of a saintly mage who never provoked Paradox in her life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:32:39-08:00","id":1037583,"title":"","content":"To clarify - even Ochemata are not resistance to normal Arcana Aggravated damage? If my Master mages try to cast Aggravated damage spells, they <i>still</i> would do Aggravated damage to it, even without employing Banes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1037537#post1037537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Ochema of the Gate would be burned by something that reaffirms the truth, or proves that the world does not &quot;need&quot; the Abyss to be a better place. Something like the ashes of a saintly mage who never provoked Paradox in her life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sarira of highest Wisdom Asended mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:38:44-08:00","id":1037591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1037583#post1037583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify - even Ochemata are not resistance to normal Arcana Aggravated damage? If my Master mages try to cast Aggravated damage spells, they <i>still</i> would do Aggravated damage to it, even without employing Banes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically yes, AFAIK.<br /> <br /> But I have a strong feeling that if an Exarch wants to deploy an Ochema for the express purpose of violence, it will probably support suitably incredible means of offense and defense, the latter which might include negating direct aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sarira of highest Wisdom Asended mage? </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, Ascension by Wisdom is still a thing, right? In that case, that might do the trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:49:29-08:00","id":1037600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1037591#post1037591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I have a strong feeling that if an Exarch wants to deploy an Ochema for the express purpose of violence, it will probably support suitably incredible means of offense and defense, the latter which might include negating direct aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Safe guard for Ochema would be having Unbreakable Numina?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD Rulebook, p. 148</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>UNBREAKABLE</b><br /> The creature is nearly indestructible. Any attack that does not score an exceptional success inflicts only a single point of bashing damage. Exceptional successes inflict damage as normal. If the creature has a weakness of some sort, attacks incorporating that weakness bypass this power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, on Gnosis 6 and Arcana 5 levels it's not that hard to score those Exceptional Success with particular Praxis spell + Willpower point spend on just 3 Success of them...<br /> <br /> True problem even is not with instant defeating of being with magic - it's that with any Aggravated damage, it's killed for good and it cannot later return to game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> From what I know, after being beaten with Aggravated damage there will be no reforming of Ochema even in Supernal / Abyssal Verge...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1037591#post1037591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, Ascension by Wisdom is still a thing, right? In that case, that might do the trick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Corpus Author Sarira, for example? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or does she not Ascended by Wisdom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:00:23-08:00","id":1037608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1037600#post1037600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Safe guard for Ochema would be having Unbreakable Numina?<br /> <br /> Still, on Gnosis 6 and Arcana 5 levels it's not that hard to score those Exceptional Success with particular Praxis spell + Willpower point spend on just 3 Success of them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that a Dread Power, not a Numen? Anyways, if you're still worried, you can easily give the Ochema a custom power that flat-out immunizes it against aggravated damage, unless in occurs from accumulated lethal damage and banes. Sorta like that Abyssal Aspects before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True problem even is not with instant defeating of being with magic - it's that with any Aggravated damage, it's killed for good and it cannot later return to game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> From what I know, after being beaten with Aggravated damage there will be no reforming of Ochema even in Supernal / Abyssal Verge... </div> </div> </div>Like someone said earlier, it's highly unlikely that a shard of a God will just sit there and let it be disintegrated. Even if your table is biased towards &quot;If it has a stat, we can kill it&quot; type of gameplay, you the Storyteller should be able to make it powerful enough not to go gently, and cunning enough to not even allow the PCs a straight brawl in the first place.<br /> <br /> And hey, we're talking about endgame-level threats here. Bending the rules a bit seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Corpus Author Sarira, for example? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or does she not Ascended by Wisdom? </div> </div> </div>Um, I think not? I haven't directly read Imperial Mysteries, so I'm not clear on the exact mechanics of Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T22:07:48-08:00","id":1037669,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> - Read Imperial Mysteries. It is a great book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T22:59:32-08:00","id":1037684,"title":"","content":"Thinking on them, I prepared custom made Dread Power / Numina / Supernal Aspect special for Ochema and Bound to use, to let them be recurring antagonists without dwarfing PCs at Masters level possibility to \u2018quickly kill\u2019 them in each confrontation.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Body of God</b><br /> This being is a \u2018shell\u2019 or physical manifestation of Supernal God. Those sub-souls are immune to simple destruction with only spells, as they need to return, again and again, to fulfill their once pointed purpose. Being cannot be killed with Aggravated damage \u2013 when she lose last point of Corpus, she reforms at nearest appropriate Supernal Verge after it\u2019s Rank in days, with Mana </i><i>equal to </i><i>her Rank. The only possible way to bypass this power is use of Bane for this being, as then death of it is permanent.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Comment:</b> So what do you think about it? Of course, my Ochema of Gate then changes \u2018Supernal\u2019 for \u2018Abyssal\u2019 in appropriate parts of description. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T03:57:35-08:00","id":1037755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1037600#post1037600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Safe guard for Ochema would be having Unbreakable Numina?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW, Unbreakable seems to apply to *attacks*, which agg-dealing spells are not. A simpler solution might be found by adapting the Mage Armor Attainments to your needs (good luck fireballing an Ochema of the General, or of the Father).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T05:02:48-08:00","id":1037774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1037755#post1037755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW, Unbreakable seems to apply to *attacks*, which agg-dealing spells are not. A simpler solution might be found by adapting the Mage Armor Attainments to your needs (good luck fireballing an Ochema of the General, or of the Father).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would debate that Fraying and Unmaking spells <i>are</i> attacks. Still, adding Mage Armor Attainments should work as great boost in defense capabilities of Ochema or Bound ( probably even \u2018normal\u2019 more powerful Supernal Beings could use them ). Here is proposed power.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Armor of Arcanum (Chosen Arcanum)</i></b><br /> <i>This being is protected by the power of Arcanum she is composed of. She is treated as having </i>Mage Armor Attainment <i>from chosen Arcanum, up to the level of her Arcana dots. Activating it for a scene is Reflexive Action. </i><i>In contrast to normal Mage Armor, being can benefit from multiple Mage Armor effect at once, if she have each </i>Armor of Arcanum<i> power for and she activated them first for the scene.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Comment:</b> I broken normal Armor Attainment limit as Supernal beings should be much more resistant compared to Awakened PCs, as they are used as bosses. Limiting multiple Armor effects to having multiple powers in the first place and need for spending Mana on them sounds as enough cost for those being. Not every Supernal Being can be made from Prime or Forces, so using secondary Arcanum can help made them more \u2018equal\u2019, appropriate to their fluff threat level.<br /> <br /> In my example, if using <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/603390-homebrew-abyssal-arcanum\">Abyss Arcanum</a> Armor from <b>malonkey</b>, our would only downgrade damage from mundane attacks, nothing about resistance on magic. With adding Prime Armor, we have nice, very hard defensive options at the cost of two Numina slots and cost of 2 Mana each combat scene. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-11-2017, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T07:21:34-08:00","id":1037825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031018-2e-ochema-and-bound?p=1037774#post1037774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would debate that Fraying and Unmaking spells <i>are</i> attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll gladly take the other side on this argument. Just not on this thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, adding Mage Armor Attainments should work as great boost in defense capabilities of Ochema or Bound ( probably even \u2018normal\u2019 more powerful Supernal Beings could use them ). Here is proposed power.<br /> <b><i>Armor of Arcanum (Chosen Arcanum)</i></b><br /> <i>This being is protected by the power of Arcanum she is composed of. She is treated as having </i>Mage Armor Attainment <i>from chosen Arcanum, up to the level of her Arcana dots. Activating it for a scene is Reflexive Action. </i><i>In contrast to normal Mage Armor, being can benefit from multiple Mage Armor effect at once, if she have each </i>Armor of Arcanum<i> power for and she activated them first for the scene.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Comment:</b> I broken normal Armor Attainment limit as Supernal beings should be much more resistant compared to Awakened PCs, as they are used as bosses. Limiting multiple Armor effects to having multiple powers in the first place and need for spending Mana on them sounds as enough cost for those being. Not every Supernal Being can be made from Prime or Forces, so using secondary Arcanum can help made them more \u2018equal\u2019, appropriate to their fluff threat level. </div> </div> </div>That seems reasonable. Attainments are a great source of power for antagonists like these - a similar power saying they can Counterspell everything thrown at them for a turn, as an Instant Action (aka, magical Dodge) also makes for a nice &quot;Aw, crap&quot; moment for your players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my example, if using <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/603390-homebrew-abyssal-arcanum\">Abyss Arcanum</a> Armor from <b>malonkey</b>, our would only downgrade damage from mundane attacks, nothing about resistance on magic. With adding Prime Armor, we have nice, very hard defensive options at the cost of two Numina slots and cost of 2 Mana each combat scene. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>I'd even go a bit further and say they have some different Attainments - in this specific example, if that Ochema of the Gate had Space 4, it could have an Attainment saying it could use its Space dots as a Withstand against hostile magic, by manipulating the Sympathy between &quot;me&quot; and &quot;that spell coming at me&quot;, or a Fate Attainment simulating a Reflexive Evil Eye spell.<br /> Ochemata are fragments of an Archmaster's Will. Make their mastery of the Arcana obvious.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T13:40:23-08:00","id":1038022,"title":"","content":"Made first draft of my Ochema of Gate to look over. Beside <b>Mage</b> 2E rules, I used previously mentioned <i>Body of God</i> and <i>Armor of Arcanum </i>powers. Also, I used <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/925972-2e-abyssal-aspects-and-numina\">Abyssal Aspects</a> for it. Still looks for one Manifestation for her \u2013 or maybe other Numina. Any comments are welcome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b><i>Mistress of Gate</i></b><br /> <b>Quote: </b><i>You need to be chained. For the worlds safety.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b>Mistress is Gate's oldest, terrifying messenger and blood hound, often working as sort of bounty hunter. Created as to sustaining Abyssal Intrusions in highly marked limits planned by Unnamable Exarch, she roams the Fallen World and bind with her chains or destroy whatever Intruder that try to pass the governing eye of her master, limiting Annanuki real influence to only deep Abyss. But there is also darker part of her mission \u2013 she hunt\u2019s every possible Hieromagus candidate, as they are said to \u2018defeat Exarchs and bury the Abyss\u2019. Mistress is said to kill across centuries till now at least dozen of possible Messiahs of Magic, only to prevent downfall of Gate itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Mistress is huge, almost 3 meters high, obsidian women-like figure resembling <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus_figurines\" target=\"_blank\">Venus figurine</a>, made entirely of sort of condensed black smoke. Most of the time she hovers few feets above of ground. On her body are numerous bolts and plats, trying to sustain <i>inside </i>her some beings who want to escape from her corpus, evidently locked in it. If not confronting her next prey, she resides in Twilight, waiting and observing without precise eyes. If finding her target, she Materialized with all dreadful Awe she invokes.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>Mistress thinks of her as \u2018Mother\u2019 to the Fallen World, protecting her \u2018children\u2019 before total chaos of full Abyss ruling over it. She is genuine concerned about the fate of the universe, but also understand that it need to stay Fallen if need to survive next eons. She can be tried to reason with, but in the end, she will hunt every danger Gate marks for her. She knows that her \u2018beloved\u2019 only want\u2019s what\u2019s best for the reality.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank (Gnosis): 6</b><br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Concerned<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Violent<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><ul><li>Destroy candidates for Hieromagus</li> <li>Stop escapes of Intrusions</li> </ul><b>Ban: </b>Unable to act against the will of the Gate<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Sarira of mage Asended by Wisdom<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Power 14, Finesse 13, Resistance 15<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>10<br /> <b>Mana: </b>50/50<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>28<br /> <b>Defense: </b>13<br /> <b>Speed: </b>30<br /> <b>Size: </b>9<br /> <b>Corpus: </b>24<br /> <br /> <b>Arcana: </b>Abyss 5, Prime 4, Mind 4, Fate 3<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Gateway (Abyss), Image, Materialize, Possess<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Body of God, Armor of Arcanum \u2013 Abyss, Armor of Arcanum \u2013 Prime, Frightening, Paradox Gorging, Presence of Paradox, Awe, Blast ( Chains ), Drain, Pathfinder, Regenerate, Prison<br /> <br /> <i>Prison</i> \u2013 As move on Grapple, being can absorb in to her the target. It takes rolling contested Resistance vs Stamina ( of target ) test \u2013 being needs only one successful roll and turn for this action. Until time of her next initiative, there is possibility of taking out the target if breaking the Grapple she has. It works as long as <i>Blast ( Chains ) </i>Numina - Range is equal to 10 yards per dot of Power and the entity does not suffer range penalties. ( In this case, it\u2019s 140 meters range. )<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Other Traits:</b><br /> Travel All Realms<br /> Take Any Shape<br /> Supernal Perfection: Gain the rote quality (re-roll failed dice) on all actions except for spellcasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-15-2017, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}